      "text": "Move To... This element is a more accessible alternative to drag & drop reordering. Press Enter or Space to move this question. Question 5 1 / 1 pts Edit this Question Delete this Question 0 numerical_question 111116653 <p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Consider a car of mass m going around a banked curve of angle&nbsp;θ</span> <span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">and radius r. What is the maximum speed at which the car can navigate the curve without sliding, where the coefficient of maximum static friction is µ<sub>s</sub>?</span></p> <p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">Consider the case where r = 55 m, m = 1400 kg,&nbsp;θ</span> <span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">= 12° and µ<sub>s</sub> = 0.65. Enter your answer in m/s.</span></p> <p><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\"><img src=\"/courses/2053526/files/118705791/preview\" alt=\"car on a banked curve\"></span></p> Consider a car of mass m going around a banked curve of angle θ and radius r. What is the maximum speed at which the car can navigate the curve without sliding, where the coefficient of maximum static friction is µs? Consider the case where r = 55 m, m = 1400 kg, θ = 12° and µs = 0.65. Enter your answer in m/s."
